==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|fornix||lang=la|arch, vault; brothel}}  Arch as in a passageway, it was customary for courtesans of the era to wait for their customers out of the rain under these archways.

{{etystub|intermediate forms: French, late latin?}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Shaped like or [[arch]] or [[vault]]; resembling a [[fornix]].

